'''bombard''' (bom- or bum-bärd′), ''v.'' [< F. ''bombarder'', batter with a bombard or cannon, < ''bombarde'', > E. ''bombard'', a cannon: see ''bombard'', ''n.'' The relation to ''bomb''<sup>2</sup> is thus only indirect.] '''I.''' ''intrans.'' To fire off bombards or cannon.

'''II.''' ''trans.'' '''1.''' To cannonade; attack with bombs; fire shot and shell at or into; batter with shot and shell.
{{smaller block|Next she [France] intends to ''bombard'' Naples.
{{right|''Burke'', Present State of Affairs.}}}}

